    "distinct_from_closed_families": [
      "Unlike RSI14, MFI14 weights direction by typical-price-times-base-volume rather than close-change magnitude.",
      "Unlike OBV, MFI14 is a bounded rolling ratio and is not a cumulative signed-volume moving average.",
      "Unlike Chaikin Money Flow, MFI14 signs raw money flow by interday typical-price direction rather than within-day close location."
    ],
    "excluded_reinterpretations": [
      "MFI14 strictly above 50 is primary; 45 and 55 are rejection-only neighbors and cannot replace it.",
